WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.546
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.546 --> 00:00:11.108
&gt;&gt; Somewhere between when we're a baby and
when we're a fully functioning

00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:16.560
member of society, we come to reach
a decision about what we're capable of.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.030
When I go around the world asking
the question, who's a great leader?

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.520
People bring up names from Gandhi,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.160
great political leaders in history,
JFK and the like.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.360
The ones who come to mind when you think
about people you admire is that they

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:40.020
are known for continuing their
development throughout their lives.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.060
Clearly, there’s a developmental process.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.390
And yet at some point, we come to the
conclusion that there are some things we

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.980
can do and some things we can’t do.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:55.006
These exceptional leaders
are not born exceptional.

00:00:55.006 --> 00:00:56.680
They didn’t know a thing.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.210
They became something over their lives and

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:02.593
the question is can you become
something over your life?

00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:07.484
Write down something you want to do to
develop yourself personally in terms of

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:10.430
development and growth mindset.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.150
Write down something that you would
like to do that would make you better at

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.811
affecting others in your organization
that way, creating a context for

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.902
others to flourish.

00:01:18.902 --> 00:01:23.356
And write down a change that you can make
in yourself that you think would impact

00:01:23.356 --> 00:01:24.920
the broader environment.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:30.800
Make them your personal commitment to
develop yourself at all three of these

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.450
levels.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.100
&gt;&gt; Transform your Approach to
Leadership Excellence and Development.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.471
Learn more about SEP,
the Stanford Executive Program.

00:01:40.471 --> 00:01:49.726
[MUSIC]

